  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundBelowTheLadder, ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "the seed decides every kernel Map <-> FinitelySupportedFunction position by the declaration it resolves to -- the join through v1.compiler.infer_env settled_type (#15118), the crossing carried by the retyped std.algebra surface plus the keyed arm the emitter asks at every render path (node_is_keyed_collection -> emit_keyed_container_type, whose applied-type arms landed on main as #15393), and every remaining leaf-spelling probe named in the FOLLOW-UP receipt below -- each executed RED keyed by declaration so a look-alike leaf named Map does not match" } },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: the leaf name Map stands for two representations of one concept. std.types Map is std.algebra FinitelySupportedFunction; a Map<K,V> annotation in a module that imports nothing defining Map (std.algebra) resolves to the KERNEL Map, host-realized. Several seed sites decide by the last name segment Map, so the two are told apart, or conflated, by spelling rather than by the declaration a position resolves to (DESIGN section 4, kernel_map_is_the_host_realization_of_the_finitely_supported_function; the Map instance of text_crossings_go_through_the_unfold).",
    "HARM: retyping the std.algebra map surface to FinitelySupportedFunction fails seed typecheck at the if-join with 'if branches resolve to incompatible types: FinitelySupportedFunction<String,X> vs Map' (scratch/algebra-map-fsf 27bda760a8, BuildBuddy 35e3f094-c706-497f-a642-7a07d75f4f20), and Map is unbound at the std.algebra resolve wall (std.keyed_row/keyed_roster infer gate). No diagnostic names the crossing: the refusal is a type-shape mismatch, not a located refusal of an undeclared crossing.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: native v2 keys Map by declaration path (v2.std.map_introduction), so the class is seed-side. The three *_primitive_delegate seams in std.algebra are where the host operation is bound; their primitive_projection rows key on declaration name, not type. Not an instance of the text class: the carrier is a value crossing between two collection declarations, with no literal.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder (no rung of the ladder guarantees a value crossing between two representations of one concept is refused unless a row declares it; the wall that decides it is a bare name comparison). CEILING: structurally guaranteed (decidable once the classifier reads the resolved declaration at every position). NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: every position that decides a kernel Map <-> FinitelySupportedFunction question keys on the resolved declaration instead of the spelled leaf -- which needs the resolve phase to carry the declaration answer, because today node_is_keyed_algebra_spelling compares container_template_algebra on the last name segment (the hardening is named in the sibling row gunbc.recurring_failure_mode emitter_keyed_container_lowering_is_keyed_by_leaf_spelling). No crossing row is added for this: the crossing is the retype, and a crossing row naming a route that does not exist is the emit_bridge_without_runtime_body class. Plus an executed RED per probe (a look-alike leaf named Map must not match) and the positive control that an imported Map and a directly spelled FinitelySupportedFunction join as one type.",
    "FOLLOW-UP (named, not silent; the sibling leaves of the join rule #15118 fixed -- DESIGN 6b, 'consolidate duplicate answers'): seed judgments still key on the leaf spelling Map and must be keyed by declaration identity. THE CENSUS IS AN IDENTITY JOIN OVER A STATED POPULATION, NOT A COUNT EQUALITY (DESIGN section 5). Review 86783 caught four named against six claimed; review 87351 caught a named site that does not exist and a hand count wrong again; review 87479 caught this file claiming a consumer the tree contradicted. So the census states a POPULATION and a PARTITION with figures machine-derived by the derivation written here -- rerun it and the classes recount themselves -- and every symbol it names is one `git grep -n <symbol> -- src/v1 ':(exclude)src/v1/stage0'` finds. POPULATION: the lines of `grep -n` for the token Map inside double quotes over src/v1/*.dag; the count is not recorded here (DESIGN section 6: name the instrument, never transcribe its output), and the classes below are what make it checkable. Files: 04_infer.dag, 04_lookup.dag, 04_types.dag, 04_resolve.dag, 05_emit.dag. PARTITION, each line assigned by its enclosing symbol, disjoint and exhaustive: CLASS (a), SIX judgments that COMPARE the leaf spelling -- the probes. CLASS (b), TEN uses that SUPPLY the kernel container PROFILE name for Map: three in v1.compiler.infer_types bare_map_node and seven in make_map_type (container_param_name calls, the constructed node name, the profile-miss diagnostic pair). A profile constructor names the built-in it builds; it is not a judgment over authored text and cannot conflate two representations. CLASS (c), ONE line supplying a rendering fallback base name: v1.compiler.emit emit_map_type (”fallback_base: Map”, src/v1/05_emit.dag). THE SIX PROBES, and the EXECUTED EVIDENCE EACH ONE ACTUALLY HAS -- stated as it is, because the previous version of this receipt named RED tests that do not exist (probes 1 to 5 have none; the only witness tests on this branch are the four listed under probes 5 and 6 and the alias pair). (1) v1.compiler.infer classify_field_recursion, the MapValueRecursion match arm (src/v1/04_infer.dag) -- NO RED on this branch, and it is out of scope for the crossing branch for the reason stated at the end of this receipt; its evidence today is the field-shape witness for the recursion it shares with List and Set. (2) and (3) v1.compiler.infer expected_collection_surface, the join probe and the completion probe on the last name segment (src/v1/04_infer.dag) -- NO RED of their own; the joins they gate are covered from the outside by a_map_aliasing_the_keyed_algebra_joins_its_declaration_as_one_type in dag/test/claim/map_annotation_resolves_by_declaration_witness.dag. (4) v1.compiler.infer expected_type_is_keyed_collection, the arity-two-or-name test (src/v1/04_infer.dag) -- NO RED of its own. (5) v1.compiler.infer_lookup map_lookup_result_type, the authored_name_at test on the product node (src/v1/04_lookup.dag) -- NO RED of its own. (6) v1.compiler.infer_resolve map_builtin_spelling, the bare-name test (src/v1/04_resolve.dag) -- added by THIS BRANCH, the subject of review 87479, and the one probe with executed look-alike evidence: a_lookalike_record_named_finitely_supported_function_aliased_as_map_is_not_the_kernel_container in dag/test/claim/map_annotation_resolves_by_declaration_witness.dag, plus the positive control an_imported_map_annotation_resolves_to_its_declaration and the fail-closed control a_map_annotation_without_an_import_refuses_as_unbound in the same file. Probe 6”s look-alike evidence lands where the decision is actually made, the alias settling in v1.compiler.types node_type_compatible, whose declared-container-alias arm returns the argument-by-argument all comparison with nothing after it (review 87307 removed two trailing disjuncts that had made it a silent widen; the_reviewer_named_element_type_pair_refuses_at_the_join in dag/test/claim/parameterized_alias_settles_by_declaration_witness.dag is the RED for that arm). PROBE 6 AT ONE CONSUMER, THE WAY REVIEW 87479 REQUIRED. `git grep -n map_builtin_spelling -- src/v1 ':(exclude)src/v1/stage0' gives the definition and ONE call, inside unimported_map_diagnostics. unimported_map_diagnostics has one call site, in the keyed-collection arm of resolve_node_bounded whose guard is `let is_map = node_is_keyed_collection(n: n, source_indices: env.source_indices)` guard; the roster only CONCATENATES AN ERROR DIAGNOSTIC there. A roster line can refuse a name but can never RENDER a look-alike as the built-in. The earlier version of this row claimed that while is_user_generic_use_site was a second consumer; fixed by DELETION rather than patching -- the leaf-name gate this branch had added at that site is gone and the arm is byte-identical to main”s (`diff` of that arm against `git show origin/main:src/v1/04_resolve.dag`: equal), because the gate was itself the leaf-name key DESIGN 4 forbids at the one site that can route a use site to the kernel realization. The declaration_ref_eq helper that gate called was added by this branch and, once the gate went, had NO consumer at all: it is deleted with it, along with the two v1.compiler.infer_env import names it alone used, so the import list is again identical to main”s (DESIGN section 3c: a declaration nothing consumes is section 2”s redundant work in its purest form). Keying that arm on the declaration -- the other option the review offered -- was tried and rejected on evidence: std.algebra FreeMonoid is declared in the CORPUS, so a declaration-identity test can answer ”this is the keyed algebra” for Map and FinitelySupportedFunction but cannot answer ”this is a built-in container” for List, Set or FreeMonoid, whose declarations are corpus-authored too; it would have made every authored FreeMonoid<T> a user generic. PROBE 6 IS A ROSTER, WHY, AND ITS RUNG: it chooses WHICH SPELLED CONTAINER NAME the unimported-use refusal covers, and the refusal's other conjunct is the module’s own visibility predicate. STATED AS MEASURED, NOT AS WISHED: this is a VISIBILITY refusal, not an unbound-name refusal — an unimported spelling can still bind through global_bare_lookup, because the gate that refuses global-bare resolution for an unlisted name (bare_free_call_requires_listed_import) covers one spelling only. So the refusal does fire where a declaration DID resolve somewhere in the index, and it is meant to: the demand is that the module name the spelling in its import list. An earlier version of this row claimed it fires only where the name resolves to nothing; that was wrong, and the harm direction is unchanged by the correction — the refusal only concatenates an error node, it can never render a look-alike as the built-in. WHAT THE OTHER SIDE OF THE DECISION ACTUALLY DOES, STATED WITHOUT INFLATION: the keyed-container admission is node_is_keyed_algebra_spelling (src/v1/04_types.dag), and it compares container_template_algebra on the last segment of the authored name — a LEAF-SPELLING CHECK, not a declaration comparison. An earlier version of this row reported it as a declaration_ref_eq comparison; it is not one, and nothing on this branch compares declaration references at that decision. The RESIDUE note in v1.compiler.types already says the same. THE KERNEL-IDENTITY ADMISSION ITSELF IS MAIN’S (0f014468652c / PR #14880, an ancestor of origin/main); what this branch adds there is not a predicate but the DECLARATION that the spelling is the host realization, gunbc.design_ruling kernel_map_is_the_host_realization_of_the_finitely_supported_function. Probe 6”s next rung is named: give the resolve phase the declaration answer, and it stops being a roster question. TWO SPELLING KEYS SIT OUTSIDE THE POPULATION AND ARE NAMED SO NOTHING IS HIDDEN: is_container_type reads container_type_arity, the carrier roster deciding which names are containers at all (a name-membership question predating this PR and unchanged by it), and node_is_keyed_algebra_spelling, whose look-alike surface is the fsk.definer stand-in and the directly-spelled receiver a_directly_spelled_finitely_supported_function_receiver_dispatches_map_keys in dag/test/claim/fsf_spelling_resolves_as_kernel_keyed_container_witness.dag; hardening it to declaration identity is the next rung in gunbc.recurring_failure_mode emitter_keyed_container_lowering_is_keyed_by_leaf_spelling. THE SIX PROBES STAY OUT OF THE CROSSING BRANCH, AND THAT IS A DECLARED CEILING, NOT SILENCE: probes 1 to 5 carry no RED because retyping them is seed work outside the crossing, and six more seed judgment changes would widen the blast radius of a branch that must rebase over the ~110-module Map import wave. This row is the trigger that keeps them tracked.",





